    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d828">

                <pb facs="0907" n="787" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg787"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Russian Ambassador to the Acting Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial Russian Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-04-10"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Commander Berlinsky solicited and obtained
                    from the Imperial Government, on account of his health, a leave of four months
                    with orders to transfer the command of the transport <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lena</hi> to the officer following him in rank.</p>
                <p>In view of the present situation of the transport <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lena</hi>, I have the honor to bring the foregoing to the knowledge of the
                    Federal Government, with the request that it inform me whether it has any
                    objection to Commander Berlinski’s taking advantage of the leave granted him in
                    view of the critical state of his health.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Count Cassini.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
